# Not a parity scenario: the horizontal keys at a permission question, for
# APPROVAL-HORIZONTAL-KEYS. fx v0.0.16 moves the choice on Left and Alt-b
# (previous) and Right and Alt-f (next) while no amendment is open, and leaves
# it on Ctrl-Left and Ctrl-Right (input_approval_runtime.zig:90-128). First an
# amendment on choice 1 with Alt-b in it (the word move there), then Down,
# which ends editing and marks choice 2, then each key with a snap after it.
# The turns, the workspace and the settings are approvals.cap's.
fx: gateway approvals-fx.json
xfx: gateway approvals-xfx.json
work approvals-ws
fx: seed approvals-fx-settings.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
wait 3
type edit the files
key Enter
wait 3
snap ask
key Tab
wait 0.4
type ab cd
wait 0.4
key M-b
wait 0.4
type z
wait 0.4
snap amend-alt-b
key Down
wait 0.4
snap down
key Left
wait 0.4
snap left
key Right
wait 0.4
snap right
key M-f
wait 0.4
snap alt-f
key M-b
wait 0.4
snap alt-b
key C-Right
wait 0.4
snap ctrl-right
key C-Left
wait 0.4
snap ctrl-left
